IE Enhanced Security Configuration (IE ESC) in the Group Policy Management Console

To get in to GPMC open PowerShell > type gpmc.msc and press Enter. This opens the Group Policy Management Console in my Domain Controler (Lab 16).

Windows Server has a feature called IE Enhanced Security Configuration (IE ESC). 
It locks down anything web-like on the server, and the GPO Settings report is displayed as a mini web page, so IE ESC blocks it. Think of it as the bouncer 
at the server’s door: it won’t even let the GPO report in without being told it’s on the guest list.

The Trusted Sites box is the guest list. It’s safe to add the entry(in Lab 16), because it’s only the local report from GPMC on DC01, not an internet site.
